---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {Content as ShellStandard} from '../data/shell-standard.md';
import PageMasthead from '../components/PageMasthead.astro';
import {Content as Grammar} from '../data/language-grammar.md';
import {Content as Coverage} from '../data/language-coverage.md';
import {Content as Forms} from '../data/language-forms.md';
import {Content as Results} from '../data/language-query-results.md';
import {Content as NativeHtml} from '../data/language-native-html.md';
import {Content as FormStyling} from '../data/language-form-styling.md';
import {Content as Decisions} from '../data/language-decisions.md';
import language from '../../../docs/language/language.json';
import snapshot from '../../../docs/language/snapshot.json';
const canonical=`https://github.com/${snapshot.repository}/tree/${snapshot.commit}`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Krigsvold UI grammar" description="Source decisions, experimental grammar, pattern contracts and framework support for Krigsvold.">
 <PageMasthead title="A grammar for the work." eyebrow="Krigsvold · Independent UI language"><div class="masthead-description"><p>Experimental grammar {language.grammarVersion}. Core {language.implementation.core.version} and Astro {language.implementation.Astro.version} below are experimental releases under the npm next tag. The <a href="/design-system/">installed package reference</a> reports this website’s actual dependencies separately.</p>
  <p>These are exact copies of the <a href={canonical}>canonical core guidance at {snapshot.commit.slice(0,7)}</a>. Native source objects take priority; translations and new application patterns carry an explicit basis.</p></div></PageMasthead>
 <div class="page-shell"><div class="container"><div class="row"><article class="col-xl-8 col-lg-9 editorial-content design-reference language-reference">

  <nav class="reference-nav" aria-label="Language sections"><a href="#page-shell">Page shell and mastheads</a><a href="#support">Framework support</a><a href="#patterns">Pattern contracts</a><a href="#grammar">Grammar</a><a href="#coverage">Coverage review</a><a href="#form-pattern">Validated forms</a><a href="#native-html">HTML anatomy</a><a href="#form-styling">Form styling</a><a href="#results-pattern">Query and selection</a><a href="#decisions">Source decisions</a></nav>
  <section id="page-shell" class="language-prose"><ShellStandard /><p><a href="https://github.com/basuhoward/krigsvold.org/tree/a3cf072c516c59ed35814e0fa153028cc91ceecd">Recorded source revision ↗</a></p></section>
  <section id="support"><h2>Framework support and maturity</h2><div class="reference-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Framework support"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Implementation</th><th scope="col">Version</th><th scope="col">Guidance snapshot status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(language.implementation).map(([name,entry])=><tr><th scope="row">{name}</th><td>{'version' in entry ? entry.version : '—'}</td><td>{entry.status}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>The source profile is opt-in. Existing palette/default contracts and Astro slots remain compatible. React event, state and focus APIs remain specific to React. See the separate <a href="/agents/">publication and agent setup record</a> for verified availability.</p></section>
  <section id="patterns"><h2>Pattern contracts and provenance</h2><div class="reference-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Pattern provenance"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Pattern</th><th scope="col">Basis</th><th scope="col">Rules</th></tr></thead><tbody>{language.patterns.map(pattern=><tr><th scope="row">{pattern.id}</th><td>{pattern.basis}</td><td>{'rules' in pattern ? pattern.rules.join('; ') : 'React specimen only; save, failure, draft protection and undo.'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>ArticleLayout adds a separate <code>contents</code> slot and retains its supporting <code>sidebar</code>. TableOfContents provides index and inline variants with depth-2 parents and depth-3 children. SiteFooter adds <code>variant="grouped"</code>, labelled groups, and host-owned identity/base slots. Its existing plain variant remains the default.</p>
  <p><a href={`${canonical}/docs/consolidation.md`}>Candidate APIs, source profile and migration guide ↗</a>. The original-site footer identity and destinations are supplied by the host, rather than embedded in the packages.</p>
  <p>Host-owned menus follow source behavior: the desktop dropdown remains white on a dark header; below 992px the submenu becomes transparent and in-flow. Astro SiteHeader remains a wrapping link header; this candidate does not introduce a dropdown controller.</p></section>
  <section id="grammar" class="language-prose"><Grammar /></section>
  <section id="coverage" class="language-prose"><Coverage /></section>
  <section id="form-pattern" class="language-prose"><Forms /></section>
  <section id="native-html" class="language-prose"><NativeHtml /></section>
  <section id="form-styling" class="language-prose"><FormStyling /></section>
  <section id="results-pattern" class="language-prose"><Results /></section>
  <section id="decisions" class="language-prose"><Decisions /></section>
  <section><h2>Remaining evidence</h2><ul>{language.openGates.map(gate=><li>{gate}</li>)}</ul><p>Machine-readable <a href="/design-system.json">package and language specification</a>. Source hashes establish provenance; they do not certify design quality or accessibility.</p></section>
 </article></div></div></div>
</BaseLayout>

